  "description": "The correctness core of offline-first sync for Rask: a hybrid logical clock, an append-only operation log, and a deterministic merge that resolves concurrent edits per field with last-writer-wins and tombstoned deletes. Pure logic with no I/O and no transport — apply the same operations in any order, more than once, on any device, and every replica lands on the same state. Conflicts are reported rather than silently resolved, so an application can tell a user what was overwritten.",
